#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368325 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc85c7ec-e94f-5cc6-a0a9-71946bc91fac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368327} {:answer/id #uuid "b6265d35-2477-5dff-9a25-0f6b76984398" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368328} {:answer/id #uuid "a0c23154-9064-52cf-9d7e-58bc4e9b6e46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368329} {:answer/id #uuid "74a203ec-054c-5784-9824-8a9ab34bfea2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368330} {:answer/id #uuid "0e12f856-7e17-572a-b616-439001e001e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6265d35-2477-5dff-9a25-0f6b76984398" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368328} :answer-field/id #uuid "20917b75-fe62-52ee-a01b-7330211086e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368326}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cbf9769b-e719-507c-b9ae-aedbdeda8205" :question/math-academy-id "q-161260" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨y+z,\\,x+z,\\,1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u-v,\\,2,\\,{v}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨0,\\,-2v,\\,0⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe're given that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨0,\\,-2v,\\,0⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨y+z,\\,x+z,\\,1⟩|}_{x=u-v\\,y=2\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨2+{v}^{2},\\,u-v+{v}^{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨2+{v}^{2},\\,u-v+{v}^{2},\\,1⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,-2v,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =(2+{v}^{2})\\cdot 0+(u-v+{v}^{2})\\cdot (-2v)+1\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-2uv+2{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨y+z,\\,x+z,\\,1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-2uv+2{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-2uv+2{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3})\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[-{u}^{2}v+2u{v}^{2}-2u{v}^{3}]_{u=0}^{u=1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-v+2{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3})\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{v}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368332 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce19b1bd-324d-57c7-be76-e8fe8afe9acf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368334} {:answer/id #uuid "24deb3bc-e5ee-5102-ab5e-233560eedbab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368335} {:answer/id #uuid "961ba168-d91b-5bb5-9344-02e1b34f322d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368336} {:answer/id #uuid "aa962c07-7205-5309-8156-c3c9859c459f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368337} {:answer/id #uuid "e6e3fd14-00cb-5b37-b59b-0c283fe3c88c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24deb3bc-e5ee-5102-ab5e-233560eedbab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368335} :answer-field/id #uuid "a674a4f2-cd96-5068-b65f-cac49a2431f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368333}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d17f424f-954b-5ecb-a437-f702f864c48b" :question/math-academy-id "q-161278" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨-x-z,\\,x-y,\\,-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,v-u,\\,-v⟩\n$$\n\nfor $-1\\le u\\le 0$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨-x-z,\\,x-y,\\,-z⟩|}_{x=u+v\\,y=v-u\\,z=-v} \\\\  & =⟨-(u+v)-(-v),\\,u+v-(v-u),\\,-(-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-u,\\,2u,\\,v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨-u,\\,2u,\\,v⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,1,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =(-u)\\cdot 1+2u\\cdot 1+v\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-u+2u+2v \\\\  & =u+2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨-x-z,\\,x-y,\\,-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(u+2v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(u+2v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}[uv+{v}^{2}]_{v=0}^{v=1}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(u+1)\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}+u]}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368339 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4777a7e-7246-5c63-b2cc-f15de086e9b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368341} {:answer/id #uuid "a14e1eae-5645-5880-a496-76966e31aba9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368342} {:answer/id #uuid "54c290e8-f182-5e4b-b01a-ec36d60e077c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368343} {:answer/id #uuid "15ac7728-cf99-549a-8a4a-51cfe0fde974" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368344} {:answer/id #uuid "2a3a7b5e-54bc-5427-921e-877957801213" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a3a7b5e-54bc-5427-921e-877957801213" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368345} :answer-field/id #uuid "1829f4ab-11f0-5efb-accd-ca19b864c308" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368340}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "defa14c1-7205-58bc-bb12-6ea263aa0092" :question/math-academy-id "q-161283" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,2,\\,-3xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u{v}^{2},\\,-1,\\,1-2u⟩\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1-2u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{v}^{2},\\,0,\\,-2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1-2u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2uv,\\,0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ {v}^{2} & 0 & -2 \\\\ 2uv & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}{v}^{2} & -2 \\\\ 2uv & 0\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}{v}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 2uv & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-4uv,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨z,\\,2,\\,-3xy⟩|}_{x=u{v}^{2}\\,y=-1\\,z=1-2u} \\\\  & =⟨1-2u,\\,2,\\,-3(u{v}^{2})(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1-2u,\\,2,\\,3u{v}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨1-2u,\\,2,\\,3u{v}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,-4uv,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =(1-2u)\\cdot 0+2\\cdot (-4uv)+3u{v}^{2}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-8uv\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,2,\\,-3xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-8uv)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-8{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}uv\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-8{\\int }_{0}^{1}u\\,\\text{d}u{\\int }_{0}^{1}v\\,\\text{d}v\\, \\\\  & =-8\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-8(\\frac{1}{2})(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368346 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9b46ce4-cfe0-5da6-bc91-65ae8c544393" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Flux Through a Surface as a Double Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06de137b-6ede-5683-9f3d-aeadb441c331" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368348} {:answer/id #uuid "bd65561d-e4ed-5243-92c9-414bb475bf74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368349} {:answer/id #uuid "60754f26-8843-55a5-8156-592e072e17dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368350} {:answer/id #uuid "b2253c7b-1411-56e9-aa8b-b031182be356" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368351} {:answer/id #uuid "dc2e42f9-839e-5bb2-927a-d7ad192cedf5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2253c7b-1411-56e9-aa8b-b031182be356" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368351} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdb1a232-d9e5-54cb-a2bc-6471682d5412" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368347}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aed9074b-c101-5f49-a2b5-c8ceda629f11" :question/math-academy-id "q-161303" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,{u}^{2}+2v,\\,{u}^{3}+3v⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}a{u}^{2}+bu+c\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}+2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{3}+3v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2u,\\,3{u}^{2}⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}+2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{3}+3v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2,\\,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2u & 3{u}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}2u & 3{u}^{2} \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3{u}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2u \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6u-6{u}^{2},\\,3{u}^{2}-3,\\,2-2u⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩{|}_{x=u+v\\,y={u}^{2}+2v\\,z={u}^{3}+3v} \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩\\cdot ⟨6u-6{u}^{2},\\,3{u}^{2}-3,\\,2-2u⟩ \\\\  & =1\\cdot (6u-6{u}^{2})+0\\cdot (3{u}^{2}-3)+2\\cdot (2-2u) \\\\  & =6u-6{u}^{2}+4-4u \\\\  & =-6{u}^{2}+2u+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-6)\\cdot {u}^{2}+2\\cdot u+4\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=-6+2+4=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368353 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9b46ce4-cfe0-5da6-bc91-65ae8c544393" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Flux Through a Surface as a Double Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2546f16f-1a49-5795-b371-db1a49986543" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368355} {:answer/id #uuid "19ef8181-4bc2-51fe-8928-ec0733bd5fb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}+uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368356} {:answer/id #uuid "a711bed6-bad2-5620-80c8-679e216bae49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{3}-{u}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368357} {:answer/id #uuid "cff6d317-0880-5cb9-b8f3-239dd3345786" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368358} {:answer/id #uuid "a2cfcb73-093b-5e1d-8d03-db28cce48510" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a711bed6-bad2-5620-80c8-679e216bae49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{3}-{u}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368357} :answer-field/id #uuid "63e38bfe-aacd-5620-bde8-95c5eb51cffd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b2c7724-366a-520d-937c-51487085d411" :question/math-academy-id "q-161384" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨{z}^{2},\\,{y}^{2},\\,x⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,v,\\,u⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-1,\\,0,\\,2u⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice we are told that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-1,\\,0,\\,2u⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨{z}^{2},\\,{y}^{2},\\,x⟩{|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y=v\\,z=u} \\\\  & =⟨{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\,0,\\,2u⟩ \\\\  & ={u}^{2}\\cdot (-1)+{v}^{2}\\cdot 0+{u}^{2}\\cdot 2u \\\\  & =2{u}^{3}-{u}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,2{u}^{3}-{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
